  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "• FIXED: Read DTOs now carry the recording-time offset on Timestamp/StartTime/EndTime — previously every read returned a UTC offset, so a record taken at midnight CEST surfaced as 22:00 the previous day to consumers reading .DateTime.\n• CHANGED: GetAggregatedHealthDataByInterval now requires a TimeZoneInfo parameter; bucket boundaries align to calendar-day starts in that zone, eliminating sync-time-of-day drift that caused \"May 1\" rows to actually count steps from 22:39 May 1 to 22:39 May 2.\n• FIXED: Daily aggregates on Android use aggregateGroupByPeriod (calendar-aware) for whole-day-multiple intervals, so DST transition days produce correct 23h/25h buckets anchored to local midnight on both sides; sub-day intervals still use the fixed-Duration path.\n• FIXED: iOS aggregate bucket StartTime/EndTime now carry the caller's time-zone offset instead of UTC +00:00, matching the Android path so consumers see \"2026-05-06 00:00 +02:00\" rather than \"2026-05-05 22:00 +00:00\" for the same instant.\n• ADDED: GetAggregatedHealthDataByCalendarPeriod<TDto>(HealthTimeRange, CalendarUnit, int count, TimeZoneInfo, ct) for variable-length calendar units (Day, Week, Month, Year). Uses java.time.Period on Android and NSDateComponents on iOS for true calendar-month / calendar-year aggregation that TimeSpan can't express.",
